\u003cshravanrn@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2027312 - Update RLBox with better crash reporting messages  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D298733\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D301427\n", "files": ["gfx/ots/RLBoxWOFF2Host.cpp", "third_party/rlbox/include/rlbox.hpp", "third_party/rlbox/include/rlbox_sandbox.hpp", "third_party/rlbox_wasm2c_sandbox/include/rlbox_wasm2c_sandbox.hpp"], "git_node": "d178ae1ae73bd064b71880a89863ac824a142675", "git_parents": ["29d76b2246d620aa9d276e49c18a2d800d0d72d3"], "node": "4894393f9c6898200c15fb6190fecaecd768b1d4", "parents": ["734bdb4069f4d583d2546482c4bdeea8c1bb209c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779238638, "git_changesets": ["d178ae1ae73bd064b71880a89863ac824a142675"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "1192": {"changesets": [{"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2025512 - Fix AsyncLogger thread safety and shutdown.  a=RyanVM\n\nJoin the internal thread in Stop() instead of detaching it, and add a\ndestructor to prevent use-after-free if AsyncLogger is destroyed while\nrunning. An mActiveLogs counter guards against racing with Stop():\nBeginLogging() uses a double-check so the spin in Stop() reliably ensures\nall in-flight pushes complete before joining.\n\nRemove AUTO_PROFILER_REGISTER_THREAD: only the calling thread needs\nregistration, not the logger thread.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D290940\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D301627\n", "files": ["dom/media/AsyncLogger.h"], "git_node": "5295d880f2a012adbb6d311a57e242a2fafba2dd", "git_parents": ["d178ae1ae73bd064b71880a89863ac824a142675"], "node": "1b7630586e8dc13ebf5c0f26f5e46b81830dc42b", "parents": ["4894393f9c6898200c15fb6190fecaecd768b1d4"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779319059, "git_changesets": ["5295d880f2a012adbb6d311a57e242a2fafba2dd"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "1193": {"changesets": [{"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2034489 - Align SharedWorker constructor with Worker.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D299973\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D301702\n", "files": ["dom/workers/sharedworkers/SharedWorker.cpp"], "git_node": "84c32b1b57f7373a67af2dc8ab856634edf9075a", "git_parents": ["5295d880f2a012adbb6d311a57e242a2fafba2dd"], "node": "3f4a524bbe13debefb90675b7302583b8c0451de", "parents": ["1b7630586e8dc13ebf5c0f26f5e46b81830dc42b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779383846, "git_changesets": ["84c32b1b57f7373a67af2dc8ab856634edf9075a"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "1194": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Moss \u003cjmoss@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041471 - Route ESR140 Windows AArch64 profile generation to 25H2 builder. r=taskgraph-reviewers,ahal a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D301912\n", "files": ["taskcluster/config.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/generate-profile/kind.yml"], "git_node": "e313dbf57304a05d1a2a1834f358585c426650c7", "git_parents": ["84c32b1b57f7373a67af2dc8ab856634edf9075a"], "node": "318db43be64cd2a041b83548b8c9f2b2e5282b12", "parents": ["3f4a524bbe13debefb90675b7302583b8c0451de"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779415120, "git_changesets": ["e313dbf57304a05d1a2a1834f358585c426650c7"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "1195": {"changesets": [{"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038465 - Use js_pod_calloc in ThreadSharedFloatArrayBufferList::Create  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D300628\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D301940\n", "files": ["dom/media/webaudio/AudioNodeEngine.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/AudioNodeEngine.h"], "git_node": "17f88bc8e5bfb86eeb2547512f00d8ebe610dd80", "git_parents": ["e313dbf57304a05d1a2a1834f358585c426650c7"], "node": "4684acd201a969dc47786b59a3a15d9db26587df", "parents": ["318db43be64cd2a041b83548b8c9f2b2e5282b12"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779420184, "git_changesets": ["17f88bc8e5bfb86eeb2547512f00d8ebe610dd80"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "1196": {"changesets": [{"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2034172 - Fix nsStandardURL::Deserialize  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D301402\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D301740\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp"], "git_node": "9843c2588b870e9a7a6823b76f677133e68a1bfd", "git_parents": ["17f88bc8e5bfb86eeb2547512f00d8ebe610dd80"], "node": "62c607390eb5d50ba087354f856e1264c358c8cf", "parents": ["4684acd201a969dc47786b59a3a15d9db26587df"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779420221, "git_changesets": ["9843c2588b870e9a7a6823b76f677133e68a1bfd"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "1197": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Moss \u003cjmoss@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041527 - Support Azure A10 WebGL renderer strings on ESR140. r=aryx a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D301954\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/test/webgl-mochitest/test_renderer_strings.html"], "git_node": "6fecaf8639ea2536502e064022992000cbc1e43e", "git_parents": ["9843c2588b870e9a7a6823b76f677133e68a1bfd"], "node": "6bb3e2bbb7b5d5858280e3f033a6bccb00e65eaf", "parents": ["62c607390eb5d50ba087354f856e1264c358c8cf"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779546946, "git_changesets": ["6fecaf8639ea2536502e064022992000cbc1e43e"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "1198": {"changesets": [{"author": "Steven Michaud \u003csmichaud@pobox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2039387 - Work around macOS 26.5 wierdness.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D301129\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302087\n", "files": ["netwerk/system/mac/nsNetworkLinkService.mm"], "git_node": "85e3f3a0c8bbadcf8789dbc23f8d3614ab87530a", "git_parents": ["6fecaf8639ea2536502e064022992000cbc1e43e"], "node": "fc627a75533995d4756715ba3601ed5957abc4e7", "parents": ["6bb3e2bbb7b5d5858280e3f033a6bccb00e65eaf"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779547023, "git_changesets": ["85e3f3a0c8bbadcf8789dbc23f8d3614ab87530a"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "1199": {"changesets": [{"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1977995 - Stop showing misleading estimates in the 'mach try' terminal output,  a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302021\n", "files": ["tools/tryselect/push.py", "tools/tryselect/selectors/fuzzy.py", "tools/tryselect/selectors/perf.py", "tools/tryselect/selectors/preview.py", "tools/tryselect/test/test_selectors.py", "tools/tryselect/util/estimates.py", "tools/tryselect/util/fzf.py", "tools/tryselect/util/manage_estimates.py"], "git_node": "10b903dd6229f2f37f34b4d58f65991d1f283028", "git_parents": ["85e3f3a0c8bbadcf8789dbc23f8d3614ab87530a"], "node": "9bf630d9a0637cc7e410e712d81d4b2530eea4fa", "parents": ["fc627a75533995d4756715ba3601ed5957abc4e7"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779547060, "git_changesets": ["10b903dd6229f2f37f34b4d58f65991d1f283028"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "1200": {"changesets": [{"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038477: Ensure a top level doc can never be a child.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D300511\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302260\n", "files": ["accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleParent.cpp"], "git_node": "22f44e61803e1799c4c2df314f79d3c94de6a686", "git_parents": ["10b903dd6229f2f37f34b4d58f65991d1f283028"], "node": "c9c53b5f5cba004f71d54dd87e5e0a657cc62c59", "parents": ["9bf630d9a0637cc7e410e712d81d4b2530eea4fa"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779728978, "git_changesets": ["22f44e61803e1799c4c2df314f79d3c94de6a686"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "1201": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr140 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings ct-logs -  a=dmeehan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302300\n", "files": ["security/ct/CTKnownLogs.h", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "security/manager/tools/log_list.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/devtools-compatibility-browsers.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": "cbece2aacbd53a67eaf582f13ac125594739e4f4", "git_parents": ["22f44e61803e1799c4c2df314f79d3c94de6a686"], "node": "c304abbd944b80759bc890434d653ae67e8af6ac", "parents": ["c9c53b5f5cba004f71d54dd87e5e0a657cc62c59"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779730939, "git_changesets": ["cbece2aacbd53a67eaf582f13ac125594739e4f4"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "1202": {"changesets": [{"author": "Makoto Kato \u003cm_kato@ga2.so-net.ne.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029326 - Handle to reach EOT. r=TYLin a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302269\n", "files": ["intl/lwbrk/LineBreaker.cpp"], "git_node": "d3866e6131ae4e4e86bb921959f79e7cd60487e0", "git_parents": ["cbece2aacbd53a67eaf582f13ac125594739e4f4"], "node": "cc268a7dab0cf4bc2b590503308828e6420f9b2b", "parents": ["c304abbd944b80759bc890434d653ae67e8af6ac"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779884651, "git_changesets": ["d3866e6131ae4e4e86bb921959f79e7cd60487e0"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "1203": {"changesets": [{"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1983032 - Don't revert PDF handler at every startup  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D263585\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302535\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_pdfviewer.js"], "git_node": "b089e10f01978ea59c906dfa5b72fd9714233ab1", "git_parents": ["d3866e6131ae4e4e86bb921959f79e7cd60487e0"], "node": "a81deac3199f9cdb640cea2cebe9dd3fa096e4d6", "parents": ["cc268a7dab0cf4bc2b590503308828e6420f9b2b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779884679, "git_changesets": ["b089e10f01978ea59c906dfa5b72fd9714233ab1"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "1204": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041887 - [esr140] Don't pass an empty filename to fontconfig.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302360\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302444\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.cpp", "layout/reftests/text-svgglyphs/reftest.list"], "git_node": "3720aaeb1e6f6eaacdffff511b492b9a19709ab2", "git_parents": ["b089e10f01978ea59c906dfa5b72fd9714233ab1"], "node": "d52badd31adbdae0f2ebd723964e5ce0766a956c", "parents": ["a81deac3199f9cdb640cea2cebe9dd3fa096e4d6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779884708, "git_changesets": ["3720aaeb1e6f6eaacdffff511b492b9a19709ab2"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "1205": {"changesets": [{"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2023902 - part 1 - Add automated tests for the copy/move ctors/assignment operators of `WidgetEvents` which have user-defined ones  a=RyanVM\n\n`WidgetMouseEvent` has a custom copy constructor which do not copy some\nmembers and that makes the copy/move constructors of the subclasses\nuse the custom copy constructor. So, the subclass's copy/move\nconstructors work differently from the default ones.\n\nSimilarly, `WidgetSimpleGestureEvent` and `WidgetTouchEvent`\nhave user-defined copy constructor which do not use the base class's\ncopy constructor.\n\nThe new tests check current behavior even though they may be\nerror-prone.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D291710\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302282\n", "files": ["widget/tests/gtest/TestWidgetEventCtors.h", "widget/tests/gtest/TestWidgetMouseEventCtors.cpp", "widget/tests/gtest/TestWidgetTouchEventCtors.cpp", "widget/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "73f4aa612bb058239b70a53f42b47e45f89e6ab1", "git_parents": ["3720aaeb1e6f6eaacdffff511b492b9a19709ab2"], "node": "f8159b53d3189fcfc334b1db1562431c2f4390bc", "parents": ["d52badd31adbdae0f2ebd723964e5ce0766a956c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2023902 - part 2 - Make `BrowserParent::SendRealMouseEvent()` do not use the copy constructor of `WidgetMouseEvent`  a=RyanVM\n\nThe source event may be a `WidgetPointerEvent`, so, we should\nassign only the proper members of `WidgetMouseEvent` and clear\nunnecessary members for the copy.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D295201\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302283\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.h"], "git_node": "e83bfcc7ef91c030f4db63d2e296f5ce737e81d9", "git_parents": ["73f4aa612bb058239b70a53f42b47e45f89e6ab1"], "node": "20ee6090753490d36ee7a8418d67e7a2d44ce8eb", "parents": ["f8159b53d3189fcfc334b1db1562431c2f4390bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2023902 - part 3 - Make `EventStateManager::HandleMiddleClickPaste()` copy the source event lossless  a=RyanVM\n\nAlthough the `WidgetPointerEvent` specific members are not used, we\nshould make a copy lossless in theory.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D295202\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302284\n", "files": ["dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "dom/events/EventStateManager.h"], "git_node": "57341f254ef94362dd892cc2125fe682b082d7c9", "git_parents": ["e83bfcc7ef91c030f4db63d2e296f5ce737e81d9"], "node": "0001284b20f7225e7f26d26f95b1e4e80ebf2208", "parents": ["20ee6090753490d36ee7a8418d67e7a2d44ce8eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2023902 - part 4 - Make `BrowserChild` dispatch `eContextMenu` event lossless  a=RyanVM\n\n`eContextMenu` is now a `WidgetPointerEvent` so that there are some\n`WidgetPointerEvent` specific members [1].\n\nHowever, `CoalescedMouseData::Coalesce` copies it as a\n`WidgetMouseEvent`. Therefore, the `WidgetPointerEvent` specific\nmembers' data is lost.\n\n1. https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/76e27fdaa88b45ffb740b6bbd21bc016cee3db25/widget/MouseEvents.h#954-957\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D295203\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302285\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/BrowserChild.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserChild.h", "dom/ipc/CoalescedMouseData.cpp", "dom/ipc/CoalescedMouseData.h", "widget/MouseEvents.h"], "git_node": "3066dd1be02b80e5ebf97e7a3b16e619fe9e839b", "git_parents": ["57341f254ef94362dd892cc2125fe682b082d7c9"], "node": "4c0ef4d9242eeaf1d087ae767cb944e2d587efb1", "parents": ["0001284b20f7225e7f26d26f95b1e4e80ebf2208"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2023902 - part 5 - Make `WidgetEvent` and its derived classes check `mClass` value at destruction in debug build  a=RyanVM\n\n`WidgetMouseEvent` is used as a concrete class but also a base class of\n`WidgetDragEvent` and `WidgetPointerEvent`. This is error-prone\nespecially when the lossy copy occurred implicitly. E.g.,\n```cpp\nWidgetPointerEvent event(...);\nWidgetMouseEvent& ref = event;\nWidgetMouseEvent copy(ref);\n```\nTo prevent the accidental lossy copy, this patch makes `WidgetEvent` and\nits subclasses assert `mClass` value at destruction. This is not cleaner\nthan asserting it in copy/move constructors and assignment operators.\nHowever, we can avoid do define user-defined copy/move constructors and\nuser-defined assignment operators which do the default things except\nthe assertion. Additionally, `WidgetMouseEvent` will have\n`MakeLossyCopy` factory method for convenience but clarifying\nintentionally doing that.\n\nAdditionally, to prevent the accidental use of the copy constructor of\n`WidgetPointerEvent` which takes `const WidgetMouseEvent&`, this adds\na new factory method, `MakeCopyFromMouseEventRef`, to\n`WidgetPointerEvent` too.\n\nNote that all non-final classes need to have copy/move constructors and\nassignment operators explicitly. Otherwise, the final classes may not be\nable to define copy/move constructors or assignment operators or need\nto use the copy constructor of the base class even in their move\nconstructors. Therefore, this patch makes them have the constructors\nand operators with `= default` at least.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D295204\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302286\n", "files": ["dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "dom/events/InternalMutationEvent.h", "dom/events/PointerEventHandler.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserChild.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/CoalescedMouseData.cpp", "widget/BasicEvents.h", "widget/ContentEvents.h", "widget/EventForwards.h", "widget/MiscEvents.h", "widget/MouseEvents.h", "widget/TextEvents.h", "widget/TouchEvents.h", "widget/nsGUIEventIPC.h"], "git_node": "6bffd03b1b569c845f5ca6e9815f1cdb81bbd7de", "git_parents": ["3066dd1be02b80e5ebf97e7a3b16e619fe9e839b"], "node": "82306cd8cac809997b108b353b106f8ea8f187f9", "parents": ["4c0ef4d9242eeaf1d087ae767cb944e2d587efb1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2023902 - part 6 - Make `nsGUIEventIPC` validate `WidgetEvent::mClass` value strictly  a=RyanVM\n\nIf it has wrong value, it's difficult to understand that how an odd\ncase caused by that occurred. So, detecting that as far as possible\nmakes it easier to understand the root cause.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D295205\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302287\n", "files": ["widget/WidgetEventImpl.cpp", "widget/nsGUIEventIPC.h"], "git_node": "c2b9c82bccd43f44fcae31efb29cc398ab9c3b04", "git_parents": ["6bffd03b1b569c845f5ca6e9815f1cdb81bbd7de"], "node": "5b838979b51cafb4df14d124e7af98154a4f1594", "parents": ["82306cd8cac809997b108b353b106f8ea8f187f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2023902 - part 7 - Get rid of unused `nsWindow::DispatchStandardEvent()` of Windows  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D289038\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302288\n", "files": ["widget/windows/nsWindow.cpp", "widget/windows/nsWindow.h"], "git_node": "005ec08ed68dc4ae1809ab57b97505c9e91fb867", "git_parents": ["c2b9c82bccd43f44fcae31efb29cc398ab9c3b04"], "node": "2392bd3f44842bd7d3a4832642aa265a2f4592c6", "parents": ["5b838979b51cafb4df14d124e7af98154a4f1594"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2034966 - Make assert sending correct event instance  a=RyanVM\n\nIt seems that the crash is caused by sending `WidgetDragEvent` or\n`WidgetPointerEvent` instance is copied and sent to a remote process\nwith a method which send `WidgetMouseEvent` instance copy. Thus, we\nwant a stack in the sender process.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D296904\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302289\n", "files": ["widget/nsGUIEventIPC.h"], "git_node": "ada3b94ecf0a553cb39b4da8c70736f659b00a16", "git_parents": ["005ec08ed68dc4ae1809ab57b97505c9e91fb867"], "node": "f6972de580ff09cce145d75a96877aadab047d28", "parents": ["2392bd3f44842bd7d3a4832642aa265a2f4592c6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2034966 - Make `CreateMouseOrPointerWidgetEvent()` consider the result instance type from the new event message  a=RyanVM\n\n`eMouseEnterIntoWidget` and `eMouseExitFromWidget` events should be\nrepresented with `WidgetMouseEvent` instances. However, the method\nuses the same class as the source event. Therefore, if the source event\nis `eContextMenu` event, it returns `WidgetPointerEvent` instance.\nThen, if the target is a remote process,\n`BrowserParent::SendRealMouseEvent()` sends the event with\n`SendRealMouseEnterExitWidgetEvent()` which takes `WidgetMouseEvent`\ninstance. Thus, `SendRealMouseEvent()` does the implicit conversion\nfrom `WidgetPointerEvent` to `WidgetMouseEvent`. Then,\n`WidgetMouseEvent` is serialized with `ePointerEventClass` value of\n`mClass`. Finally, the remote process failed to desrialize the\n`WidgetMouseEvent` because of unexpected `mClass` value.\n\nThis patch makes `CreateMouseOrPointerWidgetEvent()` considers the\nresult instance type from the new event message and assign the\n`WidgetPointerEvent` specific members only when the source event is\nalso a `WidgetPointerEvent` instance. If the result type is\n`WidgetMouseEvent` and the source is a `WidgetPointerEvent` instance,\nthe member values are not available but they shouldn't be required\nsince if they are required, we should create `ePointerEnterIntoWidget`\nand/or `ePointerExitFromWidget` or move some members from\n`WidgetPointerEvent` to `WidgetMouseEvent`.\n\nAdditionally, when I clean up the method argument, I realized that\n`WidgetEvent::AsFooEvent() const` methods are hidden if its non-const\nversion is overridden. Therefore, I fixed this issue with making a\nmacro and making each derived class use the macro to override the\nmethod. The reason why I include this change into this patch is, it\nwill help the consistency of the basic internal API between ESR 140 and\nthe newer versions if we'll uplift this patch. Then, it helps to\nbackport security patches cleanly.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297259\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302290\n", "files": ["dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "dom/events/InternalMutationEvent.h", "widget/BasicEvents.h", "widget/ContentEvents.h", "widget/MiscEvents.h", "widget/MouseEvents.h", "widget/TextEvents.h", "widget/TouchEvents.h", "widget/nsGUIEventIPC.h"], "git_node": "98ea57c9c3bdde7df7b62e8cb06c35d94fff6340", "git_parents": ["ada3b94ecf0a553cb39b4da8c70736f659b00a16"], "node": "b76cdb3b5a022f500e6a58acd4c147bbedf2a50d", "parents": ["f6972de580ff09cce145d75a96877aadab047d28"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779885064, "git_changesets": ["73f4aa612bb058239b70a53f42b47e45f89e6ab1", "e83bfcc7ef91c030f4db63d2e296f5ce737e81d9", "57341f254ef94362dd892cc2125fe682b082d7c9", "3066dd1be02b80e5ebf97e7a3b16e619fe9e839b", "6bffd03b1b569c845f5ca6e9815f1cdb81bbd7de", "c2b9c82bccd43f44fcae31efb29cc398ab9c3b04", "005ec08ed68dc4ae1809ab57b97505c9e91fb867", "ada3b94ecf0a553cb39b4da8c70736f659b00a16", "98ea57c9c3bdde7df7b62e8cb06c35d94fff6340"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "1206": {"changesets": [{"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2011842 - Filter out invalid message events.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D300226\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302923\n", "files": ["widget/EventForwards.h", "widget/WidgetEventImpl.cpp", "widget/nsGUIEventIPC.h"], "git_node": "c8e3e839e31675f3502500930b3381f184941936", "git_parents": ["98ea57c9c3bdde7df7b62e8cb06c35d94fff6340"], "node": "f3b06f46f6f43f8d4fa27d0fc140ba8878e8c934", "parents": ["b76cdb3b5a022f500e6a58acd4c147bbedf2a50d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779927538, "git_changesets": ["c8e3e839e31675f3502500930b3381f184941936"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "1207": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2039873 - Simplify SharedWorker remote type handling,  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nThis simplifies the handling of remote types for SharedWorker, by supplying the\nparent process computation with the content process remote type, and dropping\nthe content process computation.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302396\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302795\n", "files": ["dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerPrivate.cpp", "dom/workers/remoteworkers/RemoteWorkerManager.cpp", "dom/workers/remoteworkers/RemoteWorkerManager.h", "dom/workers/sharedworkers/SharedWorker.cpp", "dom/workers/sharedworkers/SharedWorkerService.cpp", "dom/workers/sharedworkers/SharedWorkerService.h"], "git_node": "23f478ccdfd1981f3ba2e1b6e821d3004af6f2e3", "git_parents": ["c8e3e839e31675f3502500930b3381f184941936"], "node": "9375f3dc4463fd171df762ec2359f2cb074db380", "parents": ["f3b06f46f6f43f8d4fa27d0fc140ba8878e8c934"], "tags": []}], "date": 1779972859, "git_changesets": ["23f478ccdfd1981f3ba2e1b6e821d3004af6f2e3"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "1208": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnical@fastmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038302 - Tidy up WebGLBuffer index cache.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D301032\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D303015\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLBuffer.cpp"], "git_node": "29b51fc9af8152647e918